  "answer": "This confirms the mechanism: `bounds.gms` in `modules/24_trade/se_trade/` applies the `p24_seTradeCapacity` bounds (set in `datainput.gms`) unconditionally to `vm_Mport.up`/`vm_Xport.up` — the switch itself gates the *data*, not the bound-setting code.\n\nThe exact configuration required is:\n\n- **`trade` module realization = `se_trade`** (`bounds.gms:127-129` only exists/executes under this realization; other trade realizations like `standard`/`capacity` don't have this SE-trade-capacity bound logic)\n- **`cm_import_EU = \"high_bio\"`** — this is the switch that activates the `$ifthen.high_bio` block in `modules/24_trade/se_trade/datainput.gms:334-364`, which populates `p24_seTradeCapacity` with the high-biomass-availability sensitivity trade flows (7.44 EJ seliqbio imports to EU-27/UKI by 2050 from SSA/LAM).\n\nSo: `--realization trade=se_trade` together with `cm_import_EU=\"high_bio\"` in the scenario config is what activates these bounds. Note the bounds file itself has no `high_bio`-specific branch — it's the upstream `datainput.gms` switch that determines whether `p24_seTradeCapacity` is populated with the high-biomass values before `bounds.gms` applies it as an upper bound.",
